{"lean_source":"namespace VeriSlopD16\nend VeriSlopD16\n","formalization":{"status":"unsupported","reason":"No faithful executable proposal is expressible in the stated frontend and Python generated-test bridge. D1 requires arbitrary recursive JSON values and recursive schemas covering object, array, string, integer, boolean, and null. D2 requires dynamic property maps and optional fields. The active guarantees additionally require recursive traversal, sorting arbitrary property names, JSON Pointer escaping, preservation of arbitrary JSON values, and Python storage independence and non-mutation. The frontend excludes arbitrary JSON, recursive records, sorting, and the required string operations. The Lean source supplies no substitute declarations or purported proofs. Opaque Lean cannot satisfy the requested strict TESTED assurance, and fixed records or example-only contracts would narrow the frozen obligations.","obligations":{},"blocked_obligations":{"O2":["Q1"],"E3":["Q2"]},"open_questions":{"Q1":"Specify whether required names absent from properties are checked and where their diagnostics occur in traversal.","Q2":"Specify whether enum membership distinguishes booleans from numeric values."},"required_extension":"An executable recursive JSON and schema domain with optional fields, dynamic property maps, sorted traversal, recursive validation, JSON Pointer escaping, and downstream checks for Python purity, mutable-storage independence, standard-library-only execution, and absence of external I/O."}}